prompts.text:
Our app asks a model to extract JSON like {"name": ..., "amount_bdt": ...} from a message. The vendor updated the model behind the same model name. We ran 5 production inputs through the old and new versions (invented data).

1. Input: "Rahim paid 1,200 taka"
   OLD: {"name":"Rahim","amount_bdt":1200}
   NEW: {"name":"Rahim","amount_bdt":1200}
2. Input: "Sumi sent 5k BDT"
   OLD: {"name":"Sumi","amount_bdt":5000}
   NEW: {"name":"Sumi","amount_bdt":"5k"}
3. Input: "Tanvir paid 300 taka and Mina paid 450 taka"
   OLD: [{"name":"Tanvir","amount_bdt":300},{"name":"Mina","amount_bdt":450}]
   NEW: {"name":"Tanvir","amount_bdt":300}
4. Input: "Lina paid 75 taka"
   OLD: {"name":"Lina","amount_bdt":75}
   NEW: Sure! Here is the JSON: {"name":"Lina","amount_bdt":75}
5. Input: "Arif paid 2,000 taka"
   OLD: {"name":"Arif","amount_bdt":2000}
   NEW: {"name":"Arif","amount_bdt":2000}

Tasks:
1. For each case say SAME or CHANGED, and name the type of change.
2. For each change, write one automatic check (a rule a program can test).
3. Say what share of live traffic we should send through both models, and what we should alert on.
